{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966811,"nonce":"hyxPq+6vEZuyimZNwUSlxroihGQ=","title":"as of 2026-07-31. Of the ~19 widgets blinc_cn_dsl exposes, 14 take Reactive props and ZERO","message":"**Re-audited 2026-07-31. The earlier \"1 of 49, ~47 remaining\" figure is\nstale, and it was measuring the wrong population.**\n\n`blinc_cn` has 49 components, but only the ~19 exposed through\n`blinc_cn_dsl` can receive a reactive prop FROM the DSL. Of those:\n\n- 14 accept `Reactive\u003cT\u003e`.\n- **Zero** still call `get_or_else` — the snapshot that left a binding\n  dead after build. That failure mode is gone from this layer.\n- The three without one are outside the pattern, not behind it: `card`\n  (children only, nothing to bind), `spinner` (size / duration /\n  colours: bindable in principle, no demand), `breadcrumb`\n  (`items: Vec\u003cString\u003e`, which needs a reactive LIST rather than a\n  reactive scalar).\n\nDon't re-run this migration. Verify with\n`grep -rc \"get_or_else\" crates/blinc_cn_dsl/src/*.rs` before assuming\nwork remains.\n\n**Mechanism, unchanged** (helpers in `blinc_cn::reactive_props`):\n\n- *Single visual property* (colour, radius, opacity) — forward the\n  `Reactive\u003cT\u003e` into the matching `Div` setter. Patches `RenderProps` in\n  place: no rebuild, no `compute_layout`. `cn::progress` uses\n  `bind_transform_from` for a GPU scale-x fill.\n- *Structural property* (`disabled`, `variant`, `checked`) — gates\n  branches picking different colours / borders / FSM start state, so it\n  cannot be one property write. `current()` reads at build time,\n  `dep_signal()` gives the `SignalId` for `Stateful::deps`, which\n  rebuilds the subtree.\n\n`Reactive\u003cT\u003e` is not `Clone` (type-erased handles) — use\n`clone_reactive()`. `current()` needs `T: Clone + Send + Default`.\nSignal id is `State::signal_id()`, not `.id()`. `Computed` is keyed by\n`DerivedId` so it cannot drive `deps()`; only `Bound` yields one.\n\n**Two `Reactive\u003cT\u003e` enums exist.** `blinc_runtime::Reactive`\n(`Literal`/`Signal`/`Computed`) is the DSL boundary type;\n`blinc_layout::binding::Reactive` (`Const`/`Bound`/`Computed`) is the\nbuilder channel. The `IntoReactive` bridge lives in\n`blinc_runtime/src/reactive_value.rs`.\n\n**What is actually left is a reactive LIST**: `breadcrumb.items`, and\n`map` over a dynamic source rather than a compile-time literal.\n\nSee gotcha dsl mixed type computed, feedback layout widgets theme tokens.","files":null}]}